* Controlled Input = when we have a "value" and an "onChange" property.
  - EX: <select value={quantity} onChange={(event) => {
                const quantitySelected = Number(event.target.value);
                setQuantity(quantitySelected);
              }}>
  
  - Make sure to move the state INSIDE the loop so each product has its own quantity selector, NOT outside, or all selectors will change when we change one quantity.

  - EX: const [quantity, setQuantity] = useState(1);

* ^ BREAKS rules of useReact hooks, since we can ONLY put them at the TOP of the component.
  - We can fix this by separating EACH product into its OWN COMPONENT.

* NPM packages for automated testing:
  - Jest
  - Vitest

* "--save-dev" = means only for development.
  - EX: npm install --save-dev vitest@3.12

* Unit Test = we test 1 piece/unit of the code.

* "npx vitest" to run tests.
  - Searches our code for all files that end with ".test.js"

  - Displays result in cmd line.

* "describe" groups tests together in a test suite.

* test suite = group of tests.

* Integration Test = test multiple units of code working together.

* render = display the component on the page.

* When testing a component, we use render.
  - EX: render(<Product />);

* npm install for integration tests.
  - npm install --save-dev @testing-library/react@16.3.0 @testing-library/jest-dom@6.6.3 @testing-library/user-event@14.6.1 jsdom@26.1.0

  - Also need to create a vitest.config.js file.

  - Also need to create a setupTests.js file.
    - Adds methods to expect(), like:
      - expect().tobeInTheDocument()
      - expect().toHaveAttribute()

* This renders a component in a fake webpage.
  - import { render } from '@testing-library/react';

* In tests we should NOT contact a real backend.
  - We can instead mock the function.

* Mock = create a fake version of a function.
  - EX: mock loadCart() since it calls from the real backend.

  - EX: const loadCart = vi.fn();

* vi.fn() = creates a fake function that does not do anything. A mock.

* "screen" lets us check the fake webpage.

* screen.getByText() searches the fake webpage screen for an element with a specific text.
  - EX: expect(
      screen.getByText('Black and Gray Athletic Cotton Socks - 6 Pairs')
    ).toBeInTheDocument();

* To search for images in tests, we need to add a test_ID to the image element.
  - EX: <div className="product-container">
      <div className="product-image-container">
        <img className="product-image"
          data-testid="product-image"
          src={product.image} />
      </div>

    - Then use this test:
      - expect(
          screen.getByTestId('product-image')
        ).toHaveAttribute('src', 'images/products/athletic-cotton-socks-6-pairs.jpg');

* We can test for user interactions like clicking a button, using this library.
  - @testing-library/user-events

  - import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event';

* Setup the user with userEvent.setup(). Following coe sets up and simulates a click.
  - user.click() = async and returns a Promise.

  - const user = userEvent.setup();
    user.click();

* Mocks entire axios package. When we import from acios, we will get a fake version of it.
  - vi.mock('axios');

* Use beforeEach() test hook to run setup code before running each test.

* "Mock the Implementation" = make the mock do whatever we want.

* Async makes a function return a Promise.

* In testing, for <Link> components to work, they need to be inside a router.
  - EX: Entire <App> is inside <BrowserRouter>

  - In testing, we wrap the component we want to test inside a MemoryRouter.

* MemoryRouter = specifically for testing.
  - EX: 
      it('displays the products correctly', () => {
        render(
          <MemoryRouter>
            <HomePage cart={[]} loadCart={loadCart} />
          </MemoryRouter>
        );
      });

* within() = lets us find things within a specific element.

* Use "getAllByTestId()" when we have MULTIPLE of the same containers with the same test ids.
  - EX: Multiple product containers.

  - screen.getAllByTestId('product-container')

* Use "findAllByTestId()" when we have to WAIT for the data to load in.
  - EX: the product containers have to be loaded in.

  - await screen.findAllByTestId('product-container')

* Run "npm install react-router@7.8.0" to fix errors for HomePage.test.jsx
